message: "If you use these programs or data, please cite them as below."
type: dataset
title: "melete-math: machine checks for nonexistence results on directed strongly regular graphs"
authors:
  - family-names: Ivanov
    given-names: Iurii
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-4137-6788"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-07"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nosdormas/melete-math"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - directed strongly regular graphs
  - nonexistence
  - rank
  - SAT certificates
  - Lean
abstract: >-
  Programs, graph catalogues, SAT certificates and Lean modules that check every
  computational step of the proofs of nonexistence of directed strongly regular
  graphs with ten parameter sets of the Hobart-Brouwer table. The Lean project
  proves the nonexistence for nine of the ten sets, for further sets and for
  complements, 28 theorems on the standard axioms only, with the Lean kernel
  checking the one stored SAT certificate; it carries the files of the Palomar
  registry of formal proofs.
